{"overview":"Camille is a courtesan in Paris. She falls deeply in love with a young man of promise, Armand Duval. When Armand's father begs her not to ruin his hope of a career and position by marrying Armand, she acquiesces and leaves her lover. However, when poverty and terminal illness overwhelm her, Camille discovers that Armand has not lost his love for her.","tagline":"Their love idyll among the spring blossoms","cast":[{"n":"Alla Nazimova","c":"Marguerite Gautier","p":"/jhFGkojzbuORf0gs1OdfeAtsvRZ.jpg","q":"Q234795"},{"n":"Rudolph Valentino","c":"Armand Duval","p":"/4g5SyNvIuknL7bH8UQNNdKj6m0u.jpg","q":"Q188692"},{"n":"Rex Cherryman","c":"Gaston Rieux","p":"/mX516Aco5TZs9SIc7ndNbgluvIx.jpg","q":"Q7319167"},{"n":"Arthur Hoyt","c":"Count de Varville","p":"/pVUoMq4jT8AgBgKbUrHH7lOLoGy.jpg","q":"Q1421566"},{"n":"Zeffie Tilbury","c":"Prudence","p":"/o1Na70AGYD8ivcc4icqT2kq0ZTG.jpg","q":"Q3575094"},{"n":"Patsy Ruth Miller","c":"Nichette","p":"/etWQtdO78xxQFLvECkeqEAzs06o.jpg","q":"Q456350"},{"n":"Elinor Oliver","c":"Nanine","p":null,"q":null},{"n":"William Orlamond","c":"Armand Duval's Father","p":"/2lWrKjMjLDLMbDGPguvaQ60YLHh.jpg","q":"Q8016366"},{"n":"Consuelo Flowerton","c":"Olympe","p":"/kX9LUQW4MFinE2ytWJJMW6sNWPY.jpg","q":null},{"n":"Edward Connelly","c":"","p":null,"q":"Q3048483"}],"country":["United States"],"language":[],"wiki":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camille_(1921_film)","qid":"Q1967524"}